#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:167
msgid ""
"The second complexity involves the decision of how to separate the "
"characters in a file into different lines. Text files explicitly determine "
"the end of each line of a file with a specific character or sequence of "
"characters. The complexity involves the particular character sequence used "
"to determine the end of each line. Different conventions have been used in "
"different computer systems. The alternative line breaking strategies are "
"explained in greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
"lineBreak\"/>, below."
msgstr ""
"Den andra utmaningen är hur filens tecken delas upp i rader. I textfiler "
"markeras slutet på varje rad med ett visst tecken eller en teckensekvens. "
"Olika datorsystem använder olika tecken för detta. Alternativen för "
"radbrytning beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
"lineBreak\"/> nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:179
msgid ""
"The third complexity involves the decision of how to separate the characters"
" in each line into separate value fields. Again, different strategies exist."
" These can be separated into two broad categories: strategies which use a "
"character or sequence of characters to separate the values, so called "
"'delimited' or 'separated' strategies, and strategies which use the position"
" of the character in the line to separate the values, so called 'fixed-"
"width' strategies. The alternative data structuring strategies are explained"
" in greater detail in <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
"dataStruct\"/>, below."
msgstr ""
"Den tredje utmaningen är hur tecknen på varje rad delas upp i olika "
"värdefält. Det finns två huvudmetoder: avgränsade värden, där ett tecken "
"eller en teckensekvens skiljer värdena åt, och värden med fast bredd, där "
"tecknens position på raden avgör var värdena börjar och slutar. Metoderna "
"beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"sect-file-textImport-complex-"
"dataStruct\"/> nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:193
msgid ""
"Fortunately, the <application>Gnumeric</application> <interface>Text "
"Import</interface> druid provides users with a way to preview the "
"information in a text file. This enables users to change the settings which "
"determine each of these three conventions until the text in the preview "
"correctly shows the contents of the data file. Therefore, while the details "
"of these three steps are complex, the practical impact on users is minimal. "
"Users can simply experiment until the file appears correct without having to"
" understand each of these complexities in detail."
msgstr ""
"Som tur är kan du med <application>Gnumeric</application> förhandsgranska "
"innehållet i textfilen med guiden <interface>Textimport</interface>. Ändra "
"inställningarna för de tre delarna tills förhandsgranskningen visar filens "
"innehåll korrekt. Därför behöver du inte kunna alla detaljer: prova dig fram"
" tills filen ser rätt ut."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:210
msgid ""
"The use of text files to store data in a structured fashion for use by "
"spreadsheet programs, and more generally all text files, require some scheme"
" to relate the binary number in the computer file itself to the characters "
"of a written language. Such schemes are called "
"<wordasword>'encodings'</wordasword>."
msgstr ""
"Textfiler som lagrar strukturerade data för kalkylprogram, och textfiler i "
"allmänhet, behöver en metod för att koppla filens binära tal till tecknen i "
"ett skriftspråk. Sådana metoder kallas <wordasword>”kodningar”</wordasword>."
